## Workbench

- Run `task workbench`, open http://localhost:8080/ and http://localhost:8080/inspected/: both answer.
- After `task workbench`, `logs/` holds a new `workbench-<time>.log` whose first line contains `msg="workbench started"` and the address.
- After Ctrl+C, the last line of that file contains `msg="workbench stopped"` and no error.

## Source in the workbench

- Run `task workbench`, open http://localhost:8080/: the table lists the 7 targets. After 10 seconds every target has SIGNALS >= 2, a green STATUS 200 and ERROR `-`.
- `curl -X PUT -d '{"mode":"outage"}' http://localhost:8080/inspected/sim/dependencies/payment-gateway`: within 10 seconds `health_ready` shows a red STATUS 503 and ERROR `-`. Set `healthy` again.
- In the raw view, JSON bodies are indented and colored, `metrics` shows colored names, labels and values, `orders` ends with "N more lines not shown", and colors are readable in light and dark mode.
- `data/source.db` exists. The log file has no `source target failing` line.
- After 15 minutes, SIGNALS of every target stays at or below 121 (10m retention / 5s interval + 1).
- Press Ctrl+C: the process exits with code 0 within 5 seconds.

